WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.760
*Intro music from the Walking Dead*

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.860
Wanna know when the zombie threat in "The Walking Dead"will end?

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.600
The producers have been leaving you clues since the very beginning.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.360
But today, we put it all together.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.280
Hello internet, welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.400
The brainiest YouTube series dedicated to film in TV.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.480
Which, unfotunately, makes us a prime target come the zombie apocalypse.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.440
So you can bet I've been watching "The Walking Dead", taking notes on how to survive in the event of that happens.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.600
Over six seasons, "The Walking Dead" has remained the biggest show on television by constantly re-inventing itself.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.180
Like in season 2, when Rick and Carl sought refuge at a farm.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.300
At first, Hershel and Rick didn't get along,

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.720
but after a while they came to understand one another.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.140
Everything was great, until zombies raided the farm,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.720
forcing Rick and Carl to flee.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:02.680
Or like the time in season 3 &amp; 4 when Rick and Carl sought refuge at a prison.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.260
At first, the prisoners and Rick didn't get along,

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.460
but then after a while they came to understand one another.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:11.540
Everything was great, until zombies raided the prison, forcing Rick and Carl to flee.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:15.780
Or like the time in season 5 &amp; 6 when Rick and Carl sought refuge in Alexandria

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.980
At first, Rick and Alexandrians didn't get along,

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.460
but after a while they came to understand one another.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.780
Everything was great, until zombies raided Alexandria forcing Rick and Carl to...

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.900
Huh, maybe I was a bit too hasty saying "re-inventing" itself.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.260
All routing aside though, are Rick, Carl and the rest

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.120
doomed to reenact the goriest version  of "Groundhog Day"

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:38.460
over and over again until they get careless and wind up trapped under a dead man in a zombie swarm?

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:43.240
I mean, look how excited we got when Eugene said he had found a cure to the outbreak, and then...

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.800
we see how well that panned out...

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.520
Are these survivors going to save 
the world by the end of the series?

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.760
Hate to break it to you, but no, no they won't.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.220
They're just average survivors trying to get by, 
not super-humans saving the world.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.480
But that's not to say they'll be 
permanently stuck in a zombie hellscape.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:03.480
In fact, I'm here to tell you today that the zombies won't be posing a threat much longer on The Walking Dead.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.400
That's right! Zombies are going extinct!

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.540
And that expiration date is approaching 
far sooner than you may realize!

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.860
Now first, I need to address one big caveat;

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.720
not all zombies were made at the same time.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:19.820
Turning into a zombie is contingent on 2 factors: When you die and/or when you're bitten.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:25.840
But it is important to note that the overwhelming number of The Walking Dead zombies were turned in the first two months of the outbreak.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.200
How do we know this? Well, Rick wakes up two months after the outbreak began,

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.560
and the world's already descended into a complete post-apocalyptic wasteland,

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.540
with only clusters of survivors left.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.220
Cities are empty!

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:40.000
You can go weeks without 
coming across another survivor.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.180
And as we learned from doctor Jenner 
at the CDC at the end of the season,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.500
this is also true for the rest of the world.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.960
Even France is overrun by zombies!

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.080
"It was the French."

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:50.280
"What?"

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.680
"They were the last ones to hold out as far as I know."

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.240
Now, zombies gain their 
power through sheer numbers.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.960
It's these hordes that have plagued the remaining survivors from the very first episode,

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.800
where Rick gets trapped in a tank 
surrounded by zombies,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.120
to the most recent season, where Rick gets trapped in an RV... surrounded by zombies.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.820
But as much as I joke about repeated 
tropes in the series,

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:12.780
it's these swarms that have shown 
the most reliable changes,

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:17.160
and these changes are our biggest clue to the way 
the whole series will end.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.640
Look closely at the evolution in the design of the zombie hordes across the seasons of the show.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:25.560
We start Season 1 with everyone pale 
and fairly well intact.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.320
By Season 3 and 4 they're looking pretty rough,

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.380
and Seasons 5 and 6, these guys are faces only a zombified mother could love.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.200
Very clearly, the creative team of The Walking Dead has been consciously making the human zombies

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.780
gradually look more and more grotesque every season.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.360
It's a conscious choice.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.480
But why?

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:49.960
Well, it's not just for scare tactics. They're doing it because these zombies are actually decomposing,

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:56.080
and like everything that decomposes, eventually they'll be nothing more than a bundle of bones and dust.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.800
Based on this information we can predict a 
timeline for when this series will end.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.200
Decomposition of a body is broken down 
into 5 general stages:

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.840
Initial Decay, Putrefaction, Black Putrefaction

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.440
Butyric Fermentation, and Dry Decay.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:15.060
Over the course of The Walking Dead's six seasons, 
the zombie hordes have slowly progressed 
through these stages.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:19.400
In the first Season, the zombies showed symptoms often associated with initial decay,

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:22.620
or as it's referred to, the "Fresh Stage" of decomposition

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.200
SUBWAY, eat fresh!

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.280
After the heart stops beating, the body goes into a complete meltdown,

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.120
breaking down on the cellular level.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.240
During this "Fresh Stage", the body's temperature drops.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:36.180
Since the heart's stopped beating, all remaining blood in the body drains to the lower portions.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.660
The skin gets tighter, turns grey.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.740
The eyes begin to sink into the skull.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:44.900
In the first season of Walking Dead, most 
zombies we see fulfil a lot of these qualities.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.820
The first zombie Rick encounters is 
a grey little girl with sunken eyes.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:52.900
The zombie horde Rick hides from 
in the tank are also, you guessed it--

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.900
pale with sunken eyes.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.880
Zombies from Season 2 through 5 of
 The Walking Dead are emblematic

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.860
of the second stage of decomposition:

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:03.280
Putrefaction - often referred to as "The Bloat Stage".

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.920
And it's not because they're feeling bloated after

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.060
eating a bunch of carbs.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:08.740
Remember--these guys are a bunch of protein eaters. No, it's because

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.860
gases start to accumulate in the body,
causing it to swell,

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:13.480
especially around the face.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.160
The eyes and tongue in particular, 
start to protrude outwards.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.240
We're not quite to Arnold Schwarzenegger "Total Recall" levels of the eye popping-ness,

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:20.760
but we're close.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.640
The gases that accumulate in the body

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.000
have nowhere to go,

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.480
causing ruptures and tears in the skin

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:31.000
much the same as the ProActiv-challenged skin of The Walking Dead Season 2 and Season 3 zombie hordes.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:34.520
It's also during this phase that the body's 
skin tone becomes marbled,

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.340
revealing a pattern of blood vessels 
in the face, abdomen, and chest.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:42.440
Look across Season 3 and you find 
yourself some "USDA Prime Marbling".

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.480
After two weeks, the skin becomes so loose

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.580
that it can easily be pulled off of a corpse.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:47.520
Does that sound familiar?

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:51.380
In Season 5, Rosita grabs a zombie 
out of the woods and, that's right,

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.080
pulls the skin right off.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.500
Which brings us to the third stage of decomposition,

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.960
"Black Putrefaction",

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.480
which is even nastier than those 
first two stages combined.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.080
During Black Putrefaction,

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:04.060
or, as it's commonly referred to, "Active Decay",

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:05.700
the skin of the corpse turns black.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.180
The corpse then flattens out like a penny, as all the gases escape.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:13.360
The internal organs liquify, 
turning the body into a soupy fluid.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.480
MM-MM-MMH.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.560
Coming soon to an overpriced Whole Foods near you.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.440
Hey- its organic, alright?

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.500
In the past 6th season of The Walking Dead,

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:24.560
zombies show clear signs of finally entering 
this 3rd stage of decomposition,

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.380
showing black discoloring of their face and torso.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.740
You can also see - or, not see,

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.680
that the eyes of many of these zombies have completely liquified,

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.980
leaving black empty chasms in their place.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.800
After this stage,  things get pretty dull.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:40.700
During the fourth stage, Buteric Fermentation, 
AKA "Advanced Decay",

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.680
the body and all remaining flesh dry out.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:44.600
And then finally, during the fifth stage,

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.640
"Dry Decay", all that remains of the body 
is just the bundle of bones.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:49.540
Now, you loyal theorists may be wondering,

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:51.540
"How do you time these post-mortem changes?"

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:56.680
"It's not like people just lay bodies out in an open field and then watch them slowly decompose, right?"

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.200
Well, actually that's exactly what happens.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.520
They're called "body farms".

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.960
But instead of growing plants, vegetables or fruit,

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.440
forensic investigators plant dead bodies,

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:07.940
and then watch them decompose over time.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:12.440
Which, little known fact, is 10 times more exciting than watching Season 2 of The Walking Dead.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:20.180
*Crickets chirping*

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.080
Body farms aid investigators in solving murders,

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.120
and establishing a time frame for the deceased.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:31.720
From this research, we know that the first stage of decomposition generally occurs between zero 
to three days post death.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.240
Putrefaction occurs four to ten days,

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:36.400
Black Putrefaction in 10 to 20 days,

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:38.860
Butyric Fermentation within 20 to 50 days,

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:43.960
and the 5th stage, Dry Decay takes 
between 50 and 350 days post-death.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:46.400
There are a number of factors, though, that actually increase

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.180
this rate of decomposition in a cadaver. 
First and foremost--

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:50.620
exposure to the elements.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:53.020
According to "Casper's Law of Decomposition"

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:54.900
- wait, are you serious?

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.420
Casper? Casper like the friendly ghost?

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.140
Who comes up with these names?

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:00.200
Scientists, real talk.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.560
I love the nerdy tongue-and-cheek 
naming conventions that you use,

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.960
but sometimes its really hard to take you seriously

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.480
when you're naming laws after 
children's cartoon characters,

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.080
or proteins after Sonic the Hedgehog.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:13.720
Anyway, "Casper's Law of Decomposition" states, quote,

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:18.200
that "A body left in the open air decomposes twice as fast as if it were immersed in water...

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:21.800
...and eight times faster than if it were buried underground." end quote.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.160
So those zombies, just by rising up out of the ground,

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:27.000
have increased their rate of decomposition, eight-fold!

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.500
The second key factor here is temperature.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:31.760
Heat accelerates the rate of cellular breakdown

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.740
and increases the rate of putrefaction.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.560
The hotter and more humid the temperature,

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.380
the quicker the body will decompose.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:39.380
So obviously, the zombies on the show

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:42.040
aren't decaying at the rate of a typical human body,

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.480
but what exactly is this zombie decay rate?

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.040
The Walking Dead, up to Season 6,

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:50.380
has taken place over 552 days 
since the zombie outbreak began.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.080
A typical human cadaver would 
have decomposed twice over,

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:55.080
at LEAST, at this point.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.720
So given that Season 6 depicts 
zombies in the latter days

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.400
of Black Putrefaction--

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.720
blackened skin, liquified organs--which tends to happen

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:04.480
around 20 days post death in a normal cadaver,

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:09.480
we can use this as correlative evidence to predict when complete zombie decay will occur.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:13.280
If 20 days equals the typical amount of time for a cadaver to reach Black Putrefaction,

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:17.120
and the same process for The Walking Dead 
zombies is 552 days.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.800
Then using some simple math, 
20 over 552 equals 50 over X

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.140
The unknown complete Dry Decay for a zombie.

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:26.260
We can predict that the zombies will 
have completely decayed

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:29.180
in 1,380 days.

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:32.540
This would be the complete life cycle 
of a zombie on The Walking Dead.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:35.320
Which means that we still have 828 days,

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:37.840
a little over two years, until the zombies become

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:40.120
nothing more than just dried up bones.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:42.120
Now, I know what you're thinking,

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:44.600
"So what? Two years? That's a really long time!"

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.700
"Look what's happened in just 
a year and a half on the show."

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:50.400
"Plus, then the zombies would 
just be skeleton zombies."

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.260
By then The Walking Dead will be hiring Ray Harryhausen.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:55.260
Sorry, that was an obscure reference.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:58.200
Ray Harryhausen was a pioneer of stop motion animation,

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.420
and perhaps his most famous scene is a skeleton battle that happens

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:03.420
in the movie Jason and the Argonauts.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:05.020
NOW YOU KNOW!

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:07.420
It's one of those lesser known pieces of cinematic history

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:09.420
that definitely deserves some celebration, so

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.260
worth mentioning here.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:13.500
But that being said, The Walking Dead 
isn't Jason and the Argonauts.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.920
The one thing that keeps the zombies 
going isn't their skeletal bodies,

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.140
it's their brains.

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:19.980
And it probably comes as no surprise

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:23.040
that its not just the external body that 
decomposes post death,

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.800
but internal organs do, too.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:27.400
And so, when in the decomposition 
timeline does the brain

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:29.600
liquify? Black Putrefaction.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.760
The very stage the zombie horde is currently in.

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.760
Rick doesn't have to shoot or stab a zombie

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:35.860
in the head to kill it.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:38.320
He just has to wait for nature to take its course.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.320
Step 1: Find another prison.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:42.720
Step 2: Build a stronger fence.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.620
Step 3: Profit!!!

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.160
So how long should Rick expect to be a dirty camper?

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.120
At the CDC in Season 1, Dr. Jenner shows them the

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.120
onset of a zombie. Per Dr. Jenner,

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:54.480
zombies don't function on the entirety of their brain,

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:56.480
just the brain stem.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.500
"The frontal lobe, the neo-cortex, the human part,

00:10:58.500 --> 00:10:59.640
that doesn't come back."

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:02.360
Thus, it's not even the entirety of the 
brain that needs to decompose,

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:03.360
just the stem.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:05.360
In a typical cadaver at room temperature,

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:08.120
this process would take a month, tops.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.540
If 20 days equals the typical amount of time for a

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:12.400
cadaver to reach Black Putrefaction,

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:15.400
and this same process for the Walkers is 552 days,

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:19.280
then using the same formula --
20 over 552 equals 30 over X,

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.380
the amount of time for zombie brain melting,

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:26.040
the brains in zombies will completely melt in 828 days.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.540
Subtracting out the time that's 
already happened on the show,

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:32.740
Rick and the gang only have to survive 276 more days

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:36.220
until the majority of zombie horde brains 
turn to complete mush.

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:38.220
However, this decay rate isn't accounting for

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:41.360
the temperature, the humidity, 
or the exposure to the outside.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:44.360
All of which increase the rate of 
decomposition tremendously.

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:46.440
So using Casper's Law of Decomposition,

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:50.020
we can predict that this process 
will happen at least 8 times faster

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:51.700
in the world of the show.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:53.980
Which means that the survivors 
have a little over a month,

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:56.660
34 days, until the zombie brains

00:11:56.760 --> 00:12:00.640
turn into pea soup and their 
lifeless corpses will be just that.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:02.600
Lifeless corpses once more.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:04.780
If that isn't enough, look no further than

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:05.440
the show itself.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:09.140
This past season has been set 
over the course of two days.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:12.300
Never before has the show jammed so much stuff

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.100
into a 48-hour period.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:16.920
Why would the show slow its timeline down so much?

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.920
Because the creators themselves know that the

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.920
zombies are on borrowed time.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.920
If you need more proof, look at the location.

